  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to local stabilisation in liberated areas in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The fight against al-Shabaab in Somalia continues to gain momentum and public support, galvanizing government efforts to exert greater control over newly recovered territory in Somalia. Security operations in the south of the country are now also conducted, and efforts to subdue al-Shabaab strongholds and consolidate gains in central Somalia are still ongoing. As counter-insurgency operations intensify, the combination of punitive actions by fleeing al-Shabaab fighters against the local communities, arising local tensions, natural resource scarcity increase population needs and require renewed and exceptional stabilisation efforts. In 2023, the Federal Government of Somalia and the EU have launched a &#xbf;Joint Operational Roadmap&#xbf;, which defines security and stabilisation as a priority and aims to deepen security cooperation between the EU and Somalia, including in the area of stabilisation in liberated areas. Within this context, the action constitutes an immediate response to support civilian stabilisation, consolidate peace, and enhance social cohesion in areas liberated from violent extremism.</narrative>
  </description>
